$\begin{aligned}
& \sin (A+B)=1 \\
& \Rightarrow A+B=\frac{\pi}{2} \quad ....\mathrm{(i)}\\
& \sin (A-B)=\frac{1}{2} \Rightarrow A-B=\frac{\pi}{6} \quad ....\mathrm{(ii)}
\end{aligned}$
Solving equation (i) and (ii) we get
$\begin{aligned}
& A=\frac{\pi}{3} \text { and } B=\frac{\pi}{6} \\
& \therefore \frac{\tan A}{\tan B}=\frac{\tan \frac{\pi}{3}}{\tan \left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right)}=\frac{\sqrt{3}}{\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}}=3: 1
\end{aligned}$
